WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.740
Identity-related administration needs extra care because small membership changes can have large security effects.

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:19.560
PowerShell can report on local users and groups, summarize administrative membership, check account state, identify disabled or locked accounts at a high level, and help review whether privileges still match operational need.

3
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:27.420
In domain environments, Active Directory adds more structure and more risk, so scripts should be scoped and reviewed with even greater discipline.

4
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.940
Group membership reporting is often safer than immediate modification.

5
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:40.680
A report can show who belongs to local Administrators groups, which service accounts have unexpected membership, or where group configuration differs from a baseline.

6
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:46.620
That visibility supports least privilege review without changing the environment on the first pass.

7
00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.360
It also gives stakeholders a concrete artifact to review before corrective action begins.

8
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.120
Bulk changes deserve friction.

9
00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:07.660
Before changing users, groups, or permissions across many systems, validate input files, confirm target scope, test against a small sample, record pre-change state, and define a correction plan.

10
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.880
Automation should not turn a typo or stale spreadsheet into a fleet-wide identity incident.

11
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:21.780
If the script changes membership, it should log what it attempted, what succeeded, what failed, and which operator or process initiated the run.

12
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.940
Documentation is part of identity administration.

13
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:32.160
Scripts should make it clear whether they are reporting, adding, removing, disabling, or changing permissions.

14
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:37.940
They should avoid hard-coded privileged accounts and should run with only the rights required for the task.

15
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:47.240
The best administrative scripts help teams keep identity control repeatable and auditable, while still preserving human review for decisions that affect access.
